# HANDOFF — Systemd References for OpenRC / Alpine Migration

Added the detection test and cached variable.

→ detect_init_system() runs systemctl --version — success = systemd, failure = OpenRC
→ IS_SYSTEMD stores the result once, reused by all future code paths
→ is_systemd() returns the cached value

Every systemd reference across `src/*.rs`, grouped by file and type, so
each item can be flagged and replaced with an OpenRC-compatible path.

---

## Abstraction: the `Actuator` trait

The `swap()` function in `src/swap.rs` is init-system-agnostic — it talks
only to the `Actuator` trait, not to systemd directly. Different implementations
drive the same swap logic:

→ `Actuator` trait (src/swap.rs:62) — four methods: `stage()`, `rollback()`,
`commit()`, `reload_restart()` — abstracts unit reconfiguration + bounce
→ `SystemdActuator` (src/swap.rs:~919) — implements `Actuator` for systemd
via drop-ins in `/etc/systemd/system` or `/run/systemd/system`
→ OpenRC impl — would implement `Actuator` via `/etc/conf.d/` edits +
`rc-service` restart, following the same swap flow
→ `swap()` (src/swap.rs:~300) uses `Actuator` for stage/rollback/reload,
so no init-system branching is needed in the swap logic itself
→ One place where init system matters inside `swap()`: the error message
at line ~436 now says "systemd" or "OpenRC" dynamically via `is_systemd()`

